Aaarrrrgghh!  I get the following error:

Problem in FUN(...X.sub.i....): Length of x (variable 2) is 5 != length of others (24151) 

Use traceback() to see the call stack

So I use traceback to see if I can figure out why S-Plus thinks that some variable is length 5.  This turns out to be the number of columns in my original data.frame that I reference in the function – the dependent and independent variable in the fixed formula and the three nested levels in the random formula.  

